  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe donor's tax rate under the TRAIN law is six percent (6%) on the total gifts exceeding Two hundred fifty thousand pesos (₱250,000) made during the calendar year.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practical terms, individuals making gifts should be aware that only the portion of their total gifts that exceeds ₱250,000 will be taxed at 6%. This exemption allows for a significant amount of gifting without incurring tax liability, which can be beneficial for estate planning and charitable contributions.",
